constant-speed (cruise) and driving-cycle emission factors in g/km.


2. Origin of the HBEFA coefficients
-----------------------------------

The coefficients are continuous reformulations (polynomial fits made by DLR)
of the Handbook Emission Factors for Road Transport (HBEFA) versions 2.1, 3.1
and 4.2. HBEFA is developed on behalf of the environmental agencies of
Germany, Switzerland, Austria, Sweden, Norway and France and coordinated by
INFRAS (Bern, Switzerland), https://www.hbefa.net/ , hbefa@infras.ch.

SUMO describes the models as (https://sumo.dlr.de/docs/Models/Emissions.html):
  "HBEFA v2.1-based: A continuous reformulation of the HBEFA v2.1 emissions
   data base (open source); HBEFA v3.1-based: A continuous reformulation of
   the HBEFA v3.1 emissions data base (open source); HBEFA v4.2-based: A
   continuous reformulation of the HBEFA v4.2 emissions data base
   (open source)"
and SUMO's NOTICE.md does not list HBEFA as third-party content, i.e. the
tables are distributed as part of SUMO under EPL-2.0 OR GPL-2.0-or-later.
No statement about an agreement with INFRAS regarding the redistribution of
these fits was found in the SUMO repository or documentation.

HBEFA itself is licensed by INFRAS (https://www.hbefa.net/en/software#licensing):
  "A simple use license is required for own (internal) use. [...]
   Commercial use: A commercial license for the Handbook of Emission Factors
   awards the right to reproduce contents of the Handbook and to integrate
   them in third-party products (software tools)."
vein does not contain HBEFA data tables or software; it contains only the
SUMO fits described above. Users needing the original HBEFA emission factors
(traffic situations, cold starts, etc.) must obtain HBEFA from INFRAS.

